a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></butt=
on></div></div></h2><p><span>Since GPT-2 (</span><a href=3D"https://d4mucfp=
ksywv.cloudfront.net/better-language-models/language_models_are_unsupervise=
d_multitask_learners.pdf">Radford et al.</a><span>) and GPT-3 (</span><a hr=
ef=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14165">Brown et al.</a><span>), we have se=
en that generative large language models (LLMs) pretrained on a general tex=
t corpus are capable of </span><em><strong>in-context learning</strong></em=
><span>, which doesn=E2=80=99t require us to further train or finetune pret=
rained LLMs if we want to perform specific or new tasks that the LLM wasn=
=E2=80=99t explicitly trained on. Instead, we can directly provide a few ex=
amples of a target task via the input prompt, as illustrated in the example=
 below.</span></p><div class=3D"captioned-image-container"><figure><a targe=
