ss.</figcaption></figure></div><p></p><p></p><p>Why use a reward model inst=
ead of training the pretained model on the human feedback directly? That's =
because involving humans in the learning process would create a bottleneck =
since we cannot obtain feedback in real-time.</p><p>As mentioned above, the=
 article is already very long, so I am deferring a more detailed explanatio=
n to a future article.</p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post">Conclusion<div c=
