0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 =
3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>=
Fine-tuning all layers of a pretrained LLM remains the gold standard for ad=
apting to new target tasks, but there are several efficient alternatives fo=
r using pretrained transformers. Methods such as feature-based approaches, =
in-context learning, and parameter-efficient finetuning techniques enable e=
ffective application of LLMs to new tasks while minimizing computational co=
sts and resources.</p><p>Moreover, reinforcement learning with human feedba=
ck (RLHF) serves as an alternative to supervised finetuning, potentially en=
hancing model performance.</p><p></p><div><hr></div><p><em><span>This magaz=
ine is a personal passion project. For those who wish to support me beyond =
